[al:新概念英语（四）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Youth]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.31]Lesson 5 | 第5课
[00:02.28]Youth | 青年
[00:09.33]How does the writer like to treat young people? | 作者喜欢怎样对待年轻人？
[00:14.44]People are always talking about 'the problem of youth'. | 人们总是在谈论“青年问题”。
[00:20.18]If there is one -- which I take leave to doubt | 如果真有这么一个问题——恕我冒昧表示怀疑，
[00:24.26]-- then it is older people who create it, not the young themselves. | ——那么它也是年长者制造出来的，而不是年轻人自己制造的。
[00:29.98]Let us get down to fundamentals and agree that the young are after all human beings | 让我们认真考虑一下问题的根本，承认年轻人毕竟也是人，
[00:36.74]-- people just like their elders. | ——是和他们的长辈一样的人。
[00:39.60]There is only one difference between an old man and a young one: | 老人和年轻人之间只有一点不同：
[00:45.00]the young man has a glorious future before him | 一个青年的辉煌未来在他前面，
[00:48.85]and the old one has a splendid future behind him: and maybe that is where the rub is. | 而一个老人的辉煌未来在他身后：也许症结就在这里。
[00:57.12]When I was a teenager, I felt that I was just young and uncertain -- | 我十几岁的时候，总觉得自己年轻而无所适从——
[01:03.42]that I was a new boy in a huge school, | 觉得自己是一所大学校里的新学生，
[01:06.66]and I would have been very pleased to be regarded as something so interesting as a problem. | 倘若能被当作一个像“问题”那样有趣的东西来看待，我会非常高兴的。
[01:13.57]For one thing, being a problem gives you a certain identity, | 首先，作为一个问题能给你某种身份，
[01:18.92]and that is one of the things the young are busily engaged in seeking. | 而这正是年轻人正忙于寻求的东西之一。
[01:24.14]I find young people exciting. | 我觉得年轻人令人振奋。
[01:27.09]They have an air of freedom, | 他们身上带有一种自由的气息，
[01:29.42]and they have not a dreary commitment to mean ambitions or love of comfort. | 他们不会为了微不足道的野心或贪图安逸而可悲地束缚自己。
[01:35.47]They are not anxious social climbers, and they have no devotion to material things. | 他们不是焦虑不安的社会攀爬者，也不迷恋物质享受。
[01:42.97]All this seems to me to link them with life and the origins of things. | 所有这些在我看来都使他们与生命和万物之源联系在一起。
[01:49.63]It's as if they were in some sense cosmic beings in violent and lovely contrast with us suburban creatures. | 从某种意义上说，他们仿佛是宇宙间的生灵，与我们这些城郊的俗物形成了鲜明而美好的对照。
[01:59.57]All that is in my mind when I meet a young person. | 每当我遇到一个年轻人，我脑子里想到的就是这些。
[02:04.36]He may be conceited, ill-mannered,  presumptuous or fatuous,  but I do not turn for protection to dreary cliches about respect for elders -- | 他可能自负无礼、放肆傲慢或愚昧无知，但我不会搬出尊重长辈的陈词滥调来保护自己——
[02:16.79]as if mere age were a reason for respect. | 仿佛仅仅年长就构成受尊重的理由似的。
[02:21.38]I accept that we are equals, and I will argue with him, as an equal, if I think he is wrong. | 我承认我们是平等的，如果我认为他错了，我会以平等的身份同他辩论。
